Buy high, get the difference!
Nanjing Real Estate Market Reappears "Price Difference Compensation" - China News Service
Yanzheng Evening News (Reporter Ma Zhubo) reported on November 10th that a decade-old "value protection agreement" has returned to Nanjing's real estate market. A property located in the New District of Jiangbei has claimed "difference refund compensation," stating that the discounts offered to other buyers before handover are greater than those from previous discounts, and the developer is willing to swap homes with buyers and refund the difference.
There are a lot of conditions in the price-guarantee agreement.
The property located in the New District of Jiangbei is called Poly Yanziyu Cloud Terrace. Mr. Sun, who was viewing the property, told the reporter that he found a "statement" last weekend when he was browsing the property.
The photographs he sent to reporters show that the developer's pledge that if the property was purchased between February 1 and February 28 from the date of the purchase and sale contract between the two parties until the delivery of the corresponding source of housing, the developer can change the house for the buyer and refund the difference if the discount on other homes in the project is greater than the discount on the previous purchase of the house (the limit is the same as the house, the same building block, the same unit, other unsold commodity houses of the same property type), the developer can change the house for the buyer and refund the difference.
Mr. Sun said that real estate consultants referred to it as a "price-lock agreement," with the aim of making buyers feel at ease to sell and not worry about the developer lowering prices for promotion. "Now they are afraid that once they buy it, the price will drop. Rushing to the sales office is no longer possible, and not bothering isn't actually heart-wrenching either."
Many home buyers believe that the terms of the bond agreement are not low, even if the buyer is willing to buy the house.
A Chinese woman who is planning to buy a new house in Jiangxi said that the price of the house should first be the same type of house, it should be in the same building, the same unit, and the buyer can compare the price of the house, so the threshold is quite high.
There are also buyers who argue that it is difficult for them to "seek redress" when purchasing properties due to asymmetry of information, as sellers may not exclude the possibility of offering additional discounts during sales.
Whether buyers can be retained remains to be seen.
Reporters inquired about real estate in Nanjing online and learned that the property was sold in November last year for a total of 252 apartment blocks with 105 square meters, 114 square meters, 129 square meters, and a total renovation sale of 39843 yuan/m2.
However, just two months later, online real estate shows that the total unsold units of this project currently stand at 157, accounting for 62.3%, with 128 units in Tower 8 having 113 unsold and 124 units in Tower 7 with 44 unsold. The total number of sold units is only 33, accounting for just 13%.
Market participants explain that "price protection agreements" also appeared in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of the previous year, the housing project Xiangtang Xiyuan on Huangshan Road West in He Xi had launched the "Price Guarantee Plan" to attract homebuyers. The details were as follows: "The company solemnly promises that if there is an increase in the discount within one year, any resulting difference will be refunded to the original owners."
Since then, in April 2011, nine properties in Nanjing have also taken out some of the housing promises to compensate for the difference in prices.
The real estate market is warming up; now it needs a ‘shot of adrenaline.’
Mr. Shen, a senior operator in the Nanjing real estate industry, said that the PPP is also one of the marketing methods for real estate companies.
He believes that today's development companies need more confidence than home buyers, and the introduction of the PPP is actually giving them a boost.
Regarding whether he can retain homebuyers, he says this depends on multiple factors such as regulatory policies and loan thresholds, and it remains to be seen at this time.
China's rescue team continues to carry out rescue operations in Turkey and has rescued four trapped individuals so far - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua News Agency February 11 – According to a notice on the website of the Ministry of Emergency Management on February 11, China's rescue team, which was searching in Turkey, dispatched three operational teams and 45 rescuers on February 10, rescuing one person who was trapped.
Two search assessment teams were dispatched to conduct an evaluation and inspection of 15 buildings on Wodabash Street.
So far, a total of four people have been rescued, five people have been identified, and life signs and risk assessments have been carried out on 25 buildings that collapsed severely.
The rescue teams will adjust their rescue forces scientifically according to the actual situation of the disaster area and on-site conditions, and carry out sustained and in-depth rescue operations.
The rescue team obtained information on assistance requests through multiple channels such as embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, verified them through various means including online inquiries and on-site searches.
Introduce the current rescue environment and building collapse situations to the Chinese Hong Kong Rescuing Team, and conduct joint search operations.
Currently coordinating with the Italian search and rescue team for regional coordination (SSC5), while sending three members to work at the 5th Regional Search and Rescue Coordination Center in charge of operations, they communicated with multiple teams from Italy, Britain, Serbia, Slovakia, Oman, etc., learned about the UN rescue organization's operation and the situation of rescue teams from various countries.
The rescue team continuously strengthens safety management and personnel support, adhering to the principle of unified command and prioritizing safety, enhancing on-site safety control, strengthening work discipline requirements, and clearly defining safety precautions.
Implement continuous rotation on-duty and sentry work systems to strengthen camp security management.
Medical personnel of the rescue team provide daily health check-ups for the members to enhance medical safeguards for key personnel. Currently, all members of the rescue team are in good health, and they are conducting disinfection and sterilization of the camp area.
After establishing the campsite, the logistics support team erected a total of 26 jumbo tents across four categories: command communication, equipment storage, medical decontamination, and living accommodation, as well as dog kennels, to ensure the provision of over 30 sets of rescue equipment at the scene.
Kim Jong-un's daughter interacts closely with his father, while his wife is left on the side.
(Comprehensive 11th Edition) North Korea held its 75th anniversary military parade on Sunday evening, with Kim Ji-won, the leader Kim Jong-un's daughter, not only attending but also standing alongside her father on the rostrum.
North Korean state media released footage on Sunday showing Kim Jong-un hugging his father affectionately, looking at him tenderly and whispering to him several times. She held her father's face with her hands and even touched his chest. The father-daughter interaction was broadcast throughout the country.
However, First Lady Li Xuezu could only retreat to the side.
In an official photo of Kim Jong-un and Lee She-sung attending dinner with their daughter Kim Jong-il on the 7th, Kim Jong-il not only rarely sits in the middle of her parents' C-seat, she also ascends the chair with Kim Jong-il at the 75th anniversary parade ceremony the following evening.
North Korean state media, CCTV of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea, later released footage of the parade, revealing more scenes of father-daughter affection.
Kim Jong-un looked at his daughter several times on the podium, the smiles on both faces never retreated and whispered in each other's ears, and Kim loved to hold his father's cheeks with his hands, and Kim Jong-un responded with a grinning smile.
Other state media images show that Kim Kumyeon touched her father’s face repeatedly with her hands when she sat on an indoor sofa with Kim Jong-un, and she touched Kim Jong-un’s chest with her hand as they walked arm in arm with their father.
First Lady Li Shui, who can only walk in the back or sit on her side, is always a few steps away from her husband and daughter.
Korean media noted that since Kim Jong-un first appeared in public last November 18, when he tested the Hwasong-17 missile, his visibility has been increasing over the past three months, and he has now appeared at official events five times so far.
North Korean state media used the highest honorifics such as "dearest heir" and "honorable heir" when mentioning Kim Chul-ah, and aired footage of her repeatedly shouting her unwavering support for the white-headed lineage from the stands while watching the military parade.
These signs have led the outside world to doubt whether Kim Jong-il has been identified as the heir to the Kim regime, with the Washington Post analyzing that Kim Jong-il is the signal that Kim Jong-il is pushing his middle-school-aged daughter to the position of successor, but there is also the view that such a judgment is still premature and that it still holds various possibilities in the case of Kim Jong-il having a son under his knee.
"The Fund E Account" Comes: CSRC Authorizes Development, All Funds under an Investor's Name Can Be Consolidated and Retrieved - Economic Observer - Professional Financial News Website
Economic Observer reporter Chen Shan How difficult is it to aggregate account information due to the proliferation of fund purchase channels?
Always forgetting about the "slush fund"?
The problems of the Kievan people will soon be resolved.
On February 10, the CSRC announced that the “Fund E Account” APP had been released on various mobile app stores and was undergoing public trial operation.
According to the introduction, the "Fund E Account" provides a one-stop service for individual investors to query information about public fund accounts and shares, aimed at addressing industry pain points such as investors forgetting their accounts or facing cumbersome querying processes.
According to data from Wind, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 fund management companies in China, managing a fund size of approximately 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 fund share registration institutions, and 411 fund sales institutions.
Each share registration institution's account system is independent and lacks an industry-wide query channel.
Industry insiders say that at the end of 2021, China had over 720 million fund investors, meaning that half of the country's population had invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to check their purchase status with different sales institutions individually, but through the “Fund E Account,” all sales channels can be queried, making it clear at a glance how many funds they hold.
What is the "Fund E Account" APP?
According to relevant documents, "Fund E Account" APP is an official mobile application developed and constructed by the China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation with approval from the China Securities Regulatory Commission, offering a one-stop query of the holdings of all market open-end fund products for investors.
Investors can conveniently and quickly track their holdings of open-end fund shares from different fund managers across various channels through the 'Fund E Account', significantly enhancing query efficiency.
Specifically, investors can query through the “Fund E Account” information including: fund account information opened with all public offering fund managers, trading account information opened with public offering fund sales institutions, and the holdings of products such as open-end shares of publicly offered securities investment funds and collective asset management plans established by securities companies where the number of investors is not subject to a limit of 200 people.
Li Yuqian, head of business operations at the Shanghai Stock Exchange Fund Evaluation Research Center, told Economic Observer that investors can get all information about their off-exchange public funds through the "Fund E Account" App in one place, helping them recover "forgotten assets." More importantly, it enables comprehensive aggregation of fund investment information across accounts for clients, allowing them to better monitor and understand their investment status in real time, accurately, and comprehensively. This helps clients optimize their fund portfolio more effectively and better plan their financial arrangements.
How to register and use?
The reporter noted that at the moment, the Apple Fund E account Apple App is already available in mobile app stores such as Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, Vivo, but the app is still in the open trial phase, registration requires filling out an invitation form and investors can contact the fund manager who holds the fund to obtain it.
A customer service personnel from a mid-to-large-sized public fund management company in Shanghai provided an invitation code consisting of six digits to an Economic Observer reporter and said, "During the app trial run phase, China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation provides each fund manager with a certain number of invitation codes. Investors call to obtain them, and we provide them all."
After the trial runs, users will no longer need invitation codes to register.
Oh, my God.
The reporter registered and conducted a query on their account via the “Fund E Account” download and use instructions posted on the official website of the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC). The entire process took just a few minutes and consisted of four main steps: user registration, real-name authentication, binding of fund accounts, and querying public offering funds.
After completing the real-name authentication, click on the "Assets" fund binding button. All fund products purchased through various fund sales platforms by the journalist will be listed in the binding option list (accounts that can be bound). After binding, one can see the total assets of the invested funds and start using the query function.
It is worth noting that the “Fund E Account” provides query services to investors and cannot be used for subscription or redemption transactions.
The data displayed in the "Fund E Account" generally corresponds to the date three trading days prior to the date of the query (T day).
For example, on February 10th, when you open the "Fund E Account," the total assets, fund shares, and net asset value displayed under the Asset page correspond to the date three trading days prior to that, which is February 7th.
