On March 29, I purchased this book through pre-order for 31 yuan, showing that it would be pushed to the device on March 31st. At that time, the Amazon website was still unable to preview the book (since it had not yet been released).
The book pushed to devices on March 31st is blank, with only "Awaiting Expectation" mentioned; meanwhile, the electronic version of the book on Amazon has been discounted to 18 yuan.
For two days, I repeatedly attempted to delete the blank books downloaded from the device and resynchronize, but was unable to obtain the electronic version of "The Essence of Business" that contains actual content. However, I noticed that the book is already available for preview on Amazon's website.
I have some thoughts to share at the moment.
1. The question of price is not the most important, the key now is how to replace the blank books on the Kindle with the actual content, instead of downloading them forever.
2. Books purchased in advance should no longer be bought, after all, in the event of a ticket skipping and downloading an empty book, the procedure would appear to be very complicated;
Hope Amazon provides a normal channel for feedback on such issues, where users can report concerns about e-book downloads or usage (this can be done through tickets or online customer service, similar to how Microsoft's official store handles such matters)
