The shipment is good.
First off, I bought it just a few days ago and found out it had gone on sale, leaving me with a negative review. It was still quite good, offering good value for money. The CPU and graphics card are sufficient to handle mainstream games and many large single-player titles. The cooling is excellent. However, the screen has some light leakage (a common problem with IPS screens), and the audio quality is not great. The hard drive isn't good (I would recommend adding an SSD myself). Yesterday, I took it to the after-sales service department for hardware inspection, and there were no issues. Windows 8. 1 comes pre-installed, which is not very user-friendly; I recommend upgrading to version 10. The seller shipped quickly, and answered all my inquiries promptly. The invoice arrived the day after I received the computer, which is good. Unfortunately, there were no gifts included.
